  "result": "Excellent! All 487 tests pass (459 + 28 new dashboard tests).\n\n## Summary\n\n**Dashboard Implementation:**\n\n**src/reports.js** - Added `dashboard(invoices, asOf)` function that returns:\n- **counts**: Object with invoice counts by status (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- **outstanding**: Total amount still due on issued or partially_paid invoices\n- **overdue**: Object with `{ count, amount }` from overdueInvoices function\n- **topCustomers**: Top 3 customers sorted by amount due, highest first, format `[{ customerId, due }]`\n\n**Example usage:**\n```javascript\nconst d = dashboard(allInvoices, '2025-03-15');\n// {\n//   counts: { draft: 2, issued: 5, partially_paid: 3, paid: 10 },\n//   outstanding: 12450,      // total due on issued/partially_paid\n//   overdue: { count: 2, amount: 2800 },\n//   topCustomers: [\n//     { customerId: 'C-002', due: 5000 },\n//     { customerId: 'C-001', due: 4200 },\n//     { customerId: 'C-003', due: 3250 }\n//   ]\n// }\n```\n\n**test/reports.test.js** - Added 28 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Structure validation (all required fields present)\n- Count accuracy for each status\n- Mixed invoice statuses\n- Outstanding calculation (ignores draft/paid, includes issued/partially_paid)\n- Overdue summary with count and amount\n- Top 3 customers aggregation and sorting\n- Edge cases: empty list, single invoice, fully paid, partially paid\n- Exclusion/inclusion logic for different statuses",
